The CIA Triad notes
To put in simply C-Confidentiality ensures that only authorized users can access specific assets or data, often enforced through strict access controls.
I-Integrity it guarantees that data is correct, authentic, and reliable, maintained through methods like encryption to prevent tampering
while A- Availability means that authorized users can access data when needed.
Why does this framework exist? I think the best way to put it is simply think about a detailed blueprint for building a very secure house.
Just as a blueprint guides builders to ensure the house is strong, safe and meets all necessary criteria.
Similarly a security framework guides organizations in setting up their security It helps them identify what they need to protect, how to protect it, and how to make sure those protections are actually working.
Without a framework, it would be like trying to build a house without any plans, you might miss crucial steps, leave vulnerabilities, and end up with a house that isn't truly safe. Frameworks provide that structured approach to make sure everyone involved knows their role in minimizing risks and keeping everything secure.
